1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:01,360
You should coach him.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,960
Are you sure?

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:04,640
Is it true

4
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:07,280
that your family and Sun's are betting
on the tennis match?

5
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,120
Who started this rumor?

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:14,480
Hey!

7
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,760
If you don’t feel better,

8
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,200
I’m not competing with you.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,720
Is this you being a good sport again?

10
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:10,960
Hey, guys!

11
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,280
Are you guys all right?

12
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:15,280
Bay!

13
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:16,880
Sun!

14
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:17,480
Bay!

15
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:17,960
Sun!

16
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,800
-Bay, what’s wrong?
-Sun!

17
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:20,360
Bay!

18
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:20,760
Sun!

19
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,360
Bay!

20
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,640
Sun, how are you feeling?

21
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,560
Hello, we have two unconscious boys

22
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,120
at Bangkok Pipat School.

23
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:28,960
-Sun!
-Bay!

24
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:29,680
-Sun!
-Bay!

25
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:39,640
Bay.

26
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,360
Bay, how are you?

27
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,440
Are you hurt anywhere?

28
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,400
Honey, go get the doctor.

29
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,640
You’re okay, right?

30
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,480
Mom, how about Sun?

31
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,240
Oh, you’re getting up?

32
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,680
Sun’s mother,

33
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,720
I’m so sorry.

34
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,040
Here, doctor.

35
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:50,840
Everyone,

36
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,600
please give me some spaceso I can do my job.

37
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,320
But, doctor, Bay has just woken up.

38
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,000
Come on, honey.

39
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,120
Let’s wait outside.

40
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,360
-Let him do his job.
-Please, everyone.

41
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:57,960
Come on.

42
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,440
I’ll be right back.

43
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:05,120
Yes.

44
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,720
Breathe in slowly.

45
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,480
Just rest for a while,

46
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,080
and you can go home.

47
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,000
Thank you, doctor.

48
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,880
Why are you hugging me?

49
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,040
Umm...

50
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,360
Umm, you’re up?

51
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,560
I’ll go get the doctor.

52
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,360
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION,MINISTRY OF CULTURE

53
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:04,240
-Hello.
-Hey.

54
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,960
Umm, how are the boys doing?

55
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,720
They’re resting.

56
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,480
But the doctor said they’ll be fine.

57
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,720
That’s good. Well...

58
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,880
Umm, the principal

59
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,360
wanted me to inform all of you

60
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,160
about...

61
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,480
the tryout for PREM’S GAME 31.

62
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,040
-Sun gets the spot?
-Bay gets the spot?

63
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,800
No, sir.

64
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,720
The principal said

65
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:38,320
she wouldn’t send anyone to join PREM’S GAME 31,

66
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,800
neither Sun nor Bay.

67
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,200
-Hey, why is that?!
-How could you say that, Kong?!

68
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,440
The principal also said,

69
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:48,360
Umm...

70
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:53,480
“Instead of seeing athletes compete with sportsmanship,

71
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,960
this has now turned into a ridiculous bet.”

72
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,120
That’s what she said.

73
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,080
Why didn’t she come to tell us herself?!

74
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,840
The principal is not available right now.

75
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:03,160
She also wanted me to tell you that

76
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,120
she hoped

77
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,360
both families

78
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:14,880
would void the contract

79
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:17,040
and never do anything like this again.

80
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,040
If you’ll excuse me.

81
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,200
Goodbye, everyone.

82
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:27,440
See what happened?

83
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:31,840
Now we’re screwed.

84
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,080
What contract?

85
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:47,600
Kong.

86
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,240
Huh?

87
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,600
What are you and the principal up to?

88
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:54,960
Nothing.

89
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,120
Well, we are.

90
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,040
But I can’t say anything right now.

91
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,160
When I can,

92
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,560
you’ll be the first to know.

93
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,600
Promise?

94
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,400
Promise.

95
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,600
Boy Boat!

96
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,320
Wow,

97
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:46,000
I haven’t seen you for ages.

98
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,360
When are you coming back to study?

99
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,680
How long are you going to take a breakfrom school?

100
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:52,680
It’s nothing.

101
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,320
I’ve just been busy these days.

102
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:55,800
I’ll catch you later.

103
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,000
Yeah?

104
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:00,080
Okay, see you later.

105
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:00,920
Yeah.

106
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,560
See you, man.

107
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:06,600
Come on.

108
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,080
Hold on,

109
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,000
you dropped out of school?

110
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,160
What happened?

111
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,000
You can tell me.

112
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,280
I’m here for you.

113
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,560
And I promise

114
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,360
I will not judge you.

115
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:30,840
But... who else knows about this?

116
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:35,880
Just my family.

117
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,520
I’m not that worried about it,

118
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,480
but my dad is.

119
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:51,680
Hmm.

120
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:52,400
Okay.

121
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,400
That’s fine.

122
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,320
If you don’t want to talk about it,

123
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:57,440
I understand.

124
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,880
And about what you were saying
to your friend,

125
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,280
I promise not to tell anyone.

126
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:08,840
Just don’t forget,

127
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,120
whenever you’re ready,

128
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:11,880
you can tell me.

129
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:13,680
I have to go.

130
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,320
See you later.

131
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,080
Kong!

132
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:23,600
When I’m ready,

133
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,040
you’ll be the first to know.

134
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,520
I promise.

135
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:28,360
Okay.

136
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:56,840
Thank you, Pa.

137
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,120
You just can’t help it, can you?

138
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,520
Well, that man...

139
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,760
He stole my dim sum recipe

140
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,320
and bullied our son.

141
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,240
You really don’t want me to fight back?

142
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,160
Stop using them as an excuse.

143
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:24,520
Whether it’s about him stealing
your recipe or what ever,

144
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,800
I don’t want to hear it.

145
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:30,200
When you’ve really lost everyone,

146
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:31,480
that’s when you’ll realize it, right?

147
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:35,760
Mom,

148
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:37,400
our ride’s here.

149
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,440
Honey,

150
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,720
did you see him at the hospital?

151
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,520
That boy was staring at our son without blinking.

152
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,400
He was trying to pick a fight,

153
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:12,480
wasn’t he?

154
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,880
Enough. Come on.

155
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,960
Go. Stop thinking about it.

156
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,440
Go.

157
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,080
So frustrating.

158
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,840
Are you sure you’re okay?

159
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,360
Yeah.

160
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,560
I’m not hurting,

161
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,160
just feeling a bit sore.

162
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:42,920
You’ve been unusually quiet.

163
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,200
You didn’t have a concussion, did you?

164
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:46,960
I’m just a bit upset.

165
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,600
Upset about what?

166
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,000
About Sun, of course.

167
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,240
Let me tell you.

168
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,120
Sun did it again.

169
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:56,400
Last time, his shoulder was hurting

170
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,120
This time he did it again.

171
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,200
He just doesn’t know his limits.

172
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,000
One day, he’ll drop dead on the court, just wait.

173
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,640
You’re worried about him?

174
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:06,600
What?!

175
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:07,920
I’m not worried.

176
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,520
I’m just annoyed.

177
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,640
If I win,

178
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,240
he’ll use this as an excuse.

179
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,920
Didn’t you and Sun use to be
best friends before?

180
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:19,320
Huh?

181
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,320
That was back then.

182
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,040
But now,

183
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:23,880
him and I,

184
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,400
we hate each other.

185
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,560
-Hate each other?
-Yeah.

186
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,400
Do you really hate each other,
or are you just pretending, huh?

187
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,320
(ADD TO YOUR STORY)

188
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:30,520
♪ I admit my heart has wanted you ♪

189
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:34,440
♪ Ever since the day I first met you ♪

190
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,560
(SAMING PHON FAI)

191
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,400
Why are you leaving so early?

192
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,560
Did you get a medical certificate yesterday?

193
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:57,480
Huh?

194
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:58,840
The medical certificate.

195
00:14:59,480 --> 00:14:59,760
I did.

196
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:00,880
Let me see.

197
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,080
Why? Are you a doctor?

198
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,240
I’m not.

199
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,360
Just let me see.

200
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:07,760
(What the hell?)

201
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:08,920
Quickly.

202
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:18,720
That’s it.

203
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,280
Hey.

204
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,960
Did the teacher ask you to get it?

205
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,520
What did the doctor say?

206
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,360
I can’t read this.

207
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,920
He said not to overexert myself,

208
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,960
not to exercise too strenuously,

209
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,240
and...

210
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,560
there are no injuries anywhere on my body.

211
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:39,840
That’s good.

212
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,360
What are you smiling about?

213
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:44,480
Nothing.

214
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:45,960
I’m not smiling.

215
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:46,760
You’re talking nonsense.

216
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,160
It’s good that you’re okay.

217
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:52,800
I’m off.

218
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:55,520
Hey, don’t you need the certificate anymore?

219
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:56,040
Nope!

220
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:59,080
Hey! What’s wrong with him?

221
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,160
My pen.

222
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,520
Hey!!

223
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,440
Sun, you’re back!

224
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,200
Oh, wow,

225
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:12,320
after yesterday’s match,
I thought you’d take a break for a month.

226
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:13,520
I know.

227
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:14,520
It was brutal.

228
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,120
Did I look that messed up yesterday?

229
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,520
Totally!

230
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,160
And...

231
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:26,760
Were you guys worried about me?

232
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:27,960
Of course, we were.

233
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,680
Why would you even ask that?

234
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:30,720
So worried that…

235
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,120
you wanted to give me a hug?

236
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:33,600
Huh?

237
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:34,760
What’d you say?

238
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:39,080
Let...let me put it like this.

239
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:40,760
If, after I woke up,

240
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,200
New Captionyou came over and hugged me,

241
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,120
why would you do that?

242
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,640
Because I was glad

243
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,360
and relieved.

244
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,840
Like, “Yay, Sun is okay!”

245
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:00,560
Oh, whatever.

246
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:01,760
You do that.

247
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,640
As for the hugging...

248
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:05,080
I’ll pass.

249
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:06,720
But I was worried about you.

250
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,520
What about…sitting next to me?

251
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:17,400
Like...waiting for me to wake up.

252
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,080
Would you do that?

253
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:21,520
Hmmm.

254
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:22,520
Don’t even.

255
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:24,320
Yesterday, after they carried you to
the hospital,

256
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:25,480
he was still asking us to go eat mala.

257
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,640
Hey! Ahem.

258
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,240
What’s wrong with you?

259
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:29,640
Were you really worried about me?

260
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,440
But at least

261
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,360
I would want to give you a hug.

262
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:35,960
Mmm.

263
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:37,640
Don’t lie to me.

264
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:41,360
Oww!

265
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:42,960
What the hell?

266
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,720
Why did you do that?

267
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:56,240
Bay!

268
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:58,600
Bay!

269
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,320
Bay!

270
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:04,440
What’s wrong with you?

271
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,840
I should be the one asking you that.

272
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,920
About the medical certificate this morning

273
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,240
and the fact that you hugged me at the hospital.

274
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:17,960
Why?

275
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,280
Is Zippo the only one allowed to hug you?

276
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,560
Don’t drag others into this.

277
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:24,760
Do you even realize

278
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,720
you’ve been acting super weird?

279
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:31,520
How?

280
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:35,240
Well, you...

281
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,640
you’ve been acting like you care about me.

282
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,080
Hey! What?

283
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,600
Maybe I knocked my head on the ground

284
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:50,160
and my brain got deprived of oxygen.

285
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,160
Bay!

286
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,760
What are you following me for?

287
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:07,600
Just answer me.

288
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:09,880
Why did you hug me?

289
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:10,760
I don’t know.

290
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:11,840
I wasn’t thinking.

291
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:12,520
I was just...

292
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,000
Just what?

293
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:41,600
Spit it out.

294
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:49,960
♪ I admit my heart has wanted you ♪

295
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,560
♪ Ever since the day I first met you ♪

296
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:03,840
The question you asked me,

297
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,440
I’d like to know the answer, too.

298
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:28,920
Oh,

299
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:30,440
you guys are here?

300
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:33,280
The principal wants to see you.

301
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:34,320
Both of you.

302
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:38,640
Yes, sir.

303
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,720
I have something to tell you.

304
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:47,680
We’ve thought this through carefully,

305
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,960
and we’ve decided that you two have to

306
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,600
compete in PREM’S GAME 31

307
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,720
in the men’s doubles event,

308
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:54,520
together.

309
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:55,560
-Huh?!
-Huh?!

310
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,760
Yesterday, Coach Kong told me

311
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,240
he saw how you performed during the tryout.

312
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,120
When you two played, you had...

313
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,440
What is it? Chemistry, Coach Kong?

314
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,120
Chemistry?

315
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,480
It’s called tactics.

316
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:08,400
Yeah.

317
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,560
When you two play together,

318
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,040
you cover each other’s weaknesses really well.

319
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,160
If you’re on the same team,

320
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,360
you could be a very strong team.

321
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:15,920
That’s called chemistry.

322
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:18,280
Eh?

323
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:19,960
You said our school wasn’t going to

324
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,800
send any representatives, didn’t you?

325
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,200
Well, I had to say that

326
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,680
so your fathers would stop interfering.

327
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,240
Anyway, I still have to send representatives

328
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,160
to PREM’S GAME 31.

329
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,160
The principal and I have decided

330
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,120
that Zippo will play singles,

331
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,160
while you two will play doubles.

332
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,360
This way, you two might stop fighting.

333
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,800
But I have to ask you

334
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:43,080
not to tell your families just yet.

335
00:21:43,120 --> 00:21:43,960
Urg,

336
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,200
even if I don’t tell him now,

337
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,520
he’ll find out anyway.

338
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:47,360
I’ll have to join the tournament,

339
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,040
go to practice,

340
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:48,440
and stuff.

341
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,400
-Right.
-I’ll have all of you

342
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,880
go to an out-of-town training camp together.

343
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,200
The whole tennis club.

344
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,640
-Huh? But...
-Out of town?

345
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,520
You can start training this evening.

346
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,200
Yes, ma’am.

347
00:21:58,800 --> 00:21:59,160
Chop-chop.

348
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:00,840
Don’t forget to sign these.

349
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:03,160
Close the door behind you.

350
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:23,320
Now,

351
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:24,960
once you’ve finished running,

352
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,680
pair up and warm up.

353
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:35,640
Hey,

354
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:37,400
you’re going to play together.

355
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:38,560
You have to practice together

356
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:40,040
so you can sync up quickly.

357
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:45,440
It’s giving enemies-to-lovers trope.

358
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,200
Hey!

359
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:52,760
-Hey!
-Hey!

360
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:54,920
I already stepped out.

361
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:58,920
What the hell are you doing?

362
00:22:58,920 --> 00:22:59,400
Yeah, yeah.

363
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,360
My bad.

364
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:01,840
One more time.

365
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:04,040
What’s wrong with these two?

366
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,080
Don’t move your knees.

367
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:12,920
Nice!

368
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:27,480
Support.

369
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:29,920
Nice.

370
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:38,720
-Yay!!
-Yay!!

371
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:37,640
Why are you still hanging out with that family’s son, huh?

372
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:39,640
But I promised Bay

373
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:40,680
we would keep playing doubles together

374
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:42,080
until we make the national team.

375
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:43,360
If you keep this up,

376
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:45,120
I’ll send you off to live with your grandpa.

377
00:25:58,320 --> 00:26:00,120
You and Bay are so in sync.

378
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:05,440
We used to play together as kids

379
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:07,360
before...

380
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:09,400
our families became rivals.

381
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:10,720
Is that true?

382
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,280
That’s why.

383
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,000
That’s why what?

384
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:18,840
It doesn’t look like you really hate each other.

385
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,480
Bay seems to really worry about you.

386
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:26,800
I don’t know.

387
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:29,960
I can’t keep up with his attitude.

388
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,400
One day he’s nice,

389
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:35,200
the next he’s mad at me again.

390
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:36,440
But during your match,

391
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:37,680
he was following your moves.

392
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:41,400
If he hated you, he wouldn’t support you that much.

393
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:44,840
I think he still sees you as his friend.

394
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:46,560
Trust me.

395
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:51,760
Actually, I’m kind of glad

396
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,120
that I get to play doubles with him again,

397
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,320
being on the same team.

398
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,560
If we compete and come back as champions,

399
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:04,760
it would be so satisfying for me.

400
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,960
Like, I wouldn’t want anything else in my life.

401
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,120
You’re gonna be champion!

402
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:10,520
Champion for sure.

403
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:11,240
You think so?

404
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,480
I know so.

405
00:27:21,840 --> 00:27:23,200
I’ll get to go home by BTS today.

406
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,240
Oops, sorry, sorry.

407
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:27,280
Sorry.

408
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:30,400
Eh?

409
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:34,200
Where is he?

410
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:39,280
I’m here to withdraw.

411
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:41,120
But you did amazing today.

412
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:43,480
If you’re worried about your family...

413
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:45,200
In fact, it’s not about my family at all.

414
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:47,440
It’s me.

415
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:48,760
I don’t want to play with him.

416
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:51,280
Besides,

417
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,400
I don’t even want to play tennis again.

418
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:58,120
What the hell is your problem?

419
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:00,200
Come talk to me outside.

420
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:03,200
Hey, hey!

421
00:28:06,800 --> 00:28:08,400
What the f*ck is wrong with you?

422
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:11,080
I just don’t want to play.

423
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,920
Would you stop being like this?

424
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:16,040
I’m tired of it.

425
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:18,000
You’re tired?

426
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:20,600
If that’s so, stop talking to me.

427
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:24,680
I really want to know.

428
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:29,640
Does getting to play doubles together again

429
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:33,640
not mean anything to you?

430
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:44,360
No.

431
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:48,560
Am I supposed to feel something?

432
00:28:50,720 --> 00:28:52,000
I quit playing a long time ago.

433
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:55,480
And what happened back then

434
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,680
doesn’t mean a thing to me.

435
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:02,480
Besides,

436
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,080
who would want to play with you?

437
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,440
You f*cking suck.

438
00:29:21,080 --> 00:29:21,360
Hey!

439
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,600
You’re crying?

440
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:36,000
Do you even care?

441
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:46,640
You’re always like this.

442
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,280
You come into my life

443
00:29:51,120 --> 00:29:52,200
then you leave me.

444
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,520
How many times have you done that to me?

445
00:29:57,680 --> 00:29:59,160
SAMING PHON FAI

446
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:08,960
I shouldn’t have let you back into my life.

447
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:27,000
Coach Kong,

448
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:30,040
I have something important to ask you.

449
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:39,040
I really want to know.

450
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,400
Do you really hate each other,

451
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,560
or are you just pretending, huh?

452
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:42,680
We do hate each other.

453
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:43,520
I think you’re just pretending to.

454
00:30:45,680 --> 00:30:46,680
Why would you think that?

455
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,560
If you really hated each other,

456
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,600
no one would try to stop you from being with Sun.

457
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,040
You chose to act like this

458
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:55,200
because it might be the only way

459
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:57,240
you can have him in your life.

460
00:30:58,320 --> 00:30:58,760
Am I right?

461
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:00,720
It’s not like that.

462
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:03,680
So, if Sun is not in your life anymore,

463
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:05,600
you will be happier, right?

464
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:09,040
You don’t have to answer me.

465
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:10,040
Just sleep on it

466
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:12,160
and find the answer for yourself.

467
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:24,880
Bay!

468
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:25,920
Bay!

469
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,200
What is it, Coach?

470
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:31,920
Are you two fighting again?

471
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:33,320
It’s nothing new.

472
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:35,680
I fight with him every day.

473
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:37,880
Why are you so excited about it?

474
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:40,480
I’m not.

475
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:42,320
It’s just...

476
00:31:44,240 --> 00:31:45,840
This time, Sun...

477
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:47,920
is dropping out of school.

478
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:51,120
Huh? Dropping out of school?

479
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:52,400
Mmm.

480
00:32:00,040 --> 00:32:01,520
SAMING PHON FAI

481
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:08,400
Is there anything wrong?

482
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:11,360
You seem distracted.

483
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:14,960
It’s nothing.

484
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:17,040
I’m just...

485
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:18,960
thinking about school.

486
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,760
Coach Kong called to tell me about it.

487
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,360
About how you want to drop out of school

488
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:31,360
and take the equivalency exam later.

489
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,600
Is there something bothering you?

490
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:39,440
Do you want to tell me?

491
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:49,760
I don’t know if I’m the reason.

492
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:53,120
If I am, I’m sorry.

493
00:32:55,280 --> 00:32:55,880
Pa,

494
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:58,240
this has nothing to do with you.

495
00:33:00,320 --> 00:33:01,760
I’m just tired. That’s all.

496
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:08,160
If I'm part of the reason you're feeling tired,

497
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:10,040
I’m really sorry.

498
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:13,800
I’m sorry about the bet as well..

499
00:33:16,520 --> 00:33:17,680
This is not about you at all.

500
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:23,240
I’m just tired. Really.

501
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:32,320
Let’s eat, Pa.

502
00:33:33,520 --> 00:33:34,360
I’ll get you some rice.

503
00:33:42,480 --> 00:33:43,440
Please eat a lot, Pa.

504
00:33:57,640 --> 00:33:57,960
Hey!

505
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:02,800
What are you doing?

506
00:34:03,120 --> 00:34:04,320
Coach Kong told me you’re dropping out.

507
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:06,640
What do you think you’re doing?

508
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:08,520
Isn’t that a bit dramatic?

509
00:34:14,640 --> 00:34:15,640
I’m exhausted, Bay.

510
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,120
I’ll just leave.

511
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:20,240
Well, I won’t let you.

512
00:34:22,640 --> 00:34:23,280
Why?

513
00:34:23,720 --> 00:34:24,520
Why? I don’t know.

514
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:25,520
But I won’t let you go.

515
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:27,480
My dad doesn’t even stop me.

516
00:34:30,200 --> 00:34:30,800
Who are you?

517
00:34:31,200 --> 00:34:32,040
Damn it, Sun.

518
00:34:33,520 --> 00:34:34,320
I’ve made up my mind.

519
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:37,480
I’m going to take the equivalency exam later.

520
00:34:39,040 --> 00:34:41,480
For now, I’m moving into a dorm near 
the athletes’ training camp.

521
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:47,000
You should be glad

522
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:52,160
you won’t have to see me anymore.

523
00:35:08,560 --> 00:35:10,360
If I told you the truth,

524
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:13,480
would you change your mind?

525
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:26,760
What truth?

526
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,120
The truth about why I left you.

527
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:37,000
SAMING PHON FAI

528
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:50,640
(It all started)

529
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,880
GET READY FOR THE MERLION DIM SUM RECIPE EVERYONE HAS BEEN LOOKING FOR
(When my dad decided to open a dim sum shop like your dad did.)

530
00:35:56,880 --> 00:35:57,920
What do you think you’re doing, Bee?!

531
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,400
I’m building my shop.

532
00:35:59,640 --> 00:36:00,280
What shop?!

533
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:02,160
It’s my own restaurant.

534
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:04,080
This is a dim sum shop just like mine!!

535
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:23,160
(Then everything just...)

536
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,200
(got out of hand.)

537
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,840
Why are you still hanging out with that family’s son, huh?

538
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,200
I told you

539
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:39,200
one day he will betray you too.

540
00:36:39,480 --> 00:36:40,760
But I promised Bay

541
00:36:40,760 --> 00:36:42,200
we would keep playing doubles together

542
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,600
until we make the national team.

543
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:44,760
Look, Sun,

544
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,440
you can get a new partner.

545
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:48,840
No, I want to play with Bay.

546
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:49,880
If you keep this up,

547
00:36:50,120 --> 00:36:51,720
I’ll send you off to live with your grandpa.

548
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:53,560
-(We used to play together)
-You’ll have to study at another school.

549
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:54,520
You won’t get to play tennis anymore.

550
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:55,360
(but then...)

551
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:57,200
(we had to go our separate ways.)

552
00:36:58,120 --> 00:36:59,600
I’m not playing tennis with you anymore.

553
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:05,760
(I was secretly hoping)

554
00:37:06,760 --> 00:37:07,640
(if one day)

555
00:37:08,240 --> 00:37:09,960
(our fathers could work through their problems,)

556
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:12,600
(we might get to play tennis together again.)

557
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,520
(But as time went by,)

558
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:24,440
(I slowly started to let go of that hope.)

559
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:27,480
(I thought being apart would be for the best.)

560
00:37:45,080 --> 00:37:47,600
POSTS.

561
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:50,960
(But when someone else actually took my place,)

562
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:52,920
(I couldn’t handle it.)

563
00:37:58,520 --> 00:37:59,120
BLOCK.

564
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:00,440
BLOCK S.SUNN_YT?

565
00:38:03,800 --> 00:38:04,600
BLOCK.

566
00:38:04,840 --> 00:38:06,080
BLOCK S.SUNN_YT?

567
00:38:07,160 --> 00:38:08,000
Next match, okay?

568
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:08,640
-Okay.
-Let’s try again.

569
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:11,920
-What the...?
-Hey!

570
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:13,240
Are you okay?

571
00:38:13,520 --> 00:38:14,200
I’m okay.

572
00:38:20,280 --> 00:38:20,960
(Before,)

573
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:23,600
(I didn’t know what my feelings were.)

574
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:25,920
What’s your f*cking problem, Bay?

575
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:27,320
What?

576
00:38:28,520 --> 00:38:29,200
What are you gonna do?

577
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:30,720
When will you stop?

578
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,760
Why do you want me to hate you so much?

579
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,280
(I just thought...)

580
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:36,720
Huh?

581
00:38:37,760 --> 00:38:39,360
You think you can hate me, right?

582
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:43,400
(it was hate.)

583
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:46,120
I f*cking hate you, too.

584
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:55,760
(I thought the two of us)

585
00:38:58,160 --> 00:38:59,840
(could never be the same again.)

586
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:05,680
I feel like I would go crazy

587
00:39:12,160 --> 00:39:13,880
every time you leave me.

588
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,480
So you...

589
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,400
choose to leave me instead?

590
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:31,280
I’m so afraid.

591
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,640
I’m afraid that...

592
00:39:37,200 --> 00:39:38,640
if we love each other,

593
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,280
someone will take you away from me some day.

594
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:53,040
I just want you in my life.

595
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,840
Even if we have to be enemies, 
I can take it.

596
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:08,320
I really, really like you, Sun.

597
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:13,600
I’m sorry

598
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:16,240
it took me this long to realize.

599
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:22,760
But after hearing this,

600
00:40:24,680 --> 00:40:25,800
will you still disappear?

601
00:40:43,200 --> 00:40:45,040
When you said you love me,

602
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:51,480
what kind of love was it?

603
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:55,960
♪ I admit my heart has wanted you ♪

604
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:59,640
♪ Ever since the day I first met you ♪

605
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:03,360
♪ You filled the missing space beside me ♪

606
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:07,240
♪ Now everything means more than it used to be ♪

607
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:18,360
2 YEARS AGO

608
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:20,120
Ouch!

609
00:41:21,600 --> 00:41:22,360
Damn.

610
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:24,320
What the hell do you think you’re doing?

611
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:26,720
Stop pulling pranks on my partners.

612
00:41:27,280 --> 00:41:28,480
No one wants to play tennis with me now.

613
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:32,160
Serves you right.

614
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,760
You’re trying to ruin my future?

615
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:36,000
Huh?

616
00:41:37,240 --> 00:41:37,560
Mmm.

617
00:41:37,840 --> 00:41:38,920
Oww! Damn it.

618
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:39,720
If no one’s playing doubles with you,

619
00:41:39,720 --> 00:41:40,560
go play singles instead.

620
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:42,160
Don’t be dumb.

621
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:46,440
Your dad is dumb.

622
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:46,880
Hey.

623
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:49,240
Why?

624
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:51,880
You can win on your own?

625
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:53,400
You’re afraid you’ll lose?

626
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:54,720
Are you a loser?

627
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:55,960
Huh? Loser.

628
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:57,520
-You suck.
-Shut the hell up!

629
00:41:57,680 --> 00:41:58,920
-You suck.
-Assh*le! Don’t run away.

630
00:41:59,080 --> 00:42:00,000
-Loser.
-Get back here.

631
00:42:00,120 --> 00:42:01,240
-Come on.
-Stop running away then.

632
00:42:03,080 --> 00:42:04,120
You can’t catch me.

633
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:05,360
Ha, loser.

634
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:06,640
Ha,

635
00:42:06,880 --> 00:42:08,160
loser, loser, loser.

636
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:09,600
Oh, sht.

637
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:28,040
Can you just play singles from now on

638
00:42:29,520 --> 00:42:30,160
for me?

639
00:42:41,640 --> 00:42:42,360
(What’s wrong?)

640
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:44,000
(Why are you here alone?)

641
00:42:44,320 --> 00:42:45,240
(What’s going on with you?)

642
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:46,840
(You’ve been avoiding me all day.)

643
00:42:49,760 --> 00:42:51,000
(Well, I don’t know how to act.)

644
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,920
(I don’t even know how I feel.)

645
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:54,360
(Do you like me, Sun?)

646
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,360
(If you like me too,)

647
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:57,760
(I’m willing to get through any obstacle.)

648
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:59,920
(It feels great knowing that you like me.)

649
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:02,600
(But does this mean I like you too?)

650
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:04,160
(I’m still not sure.)

651
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,760
(Will you let me try to win you over)

652
00:43:07,840 --> 00:43:08,760
(until you’re sure about your feelings?)

653
00:43:09,040 --> 00:43:12,520
♪ I admit my heart has wanted you ♪

654
00:43:12,920 --> 00:43:16,360
♪ Ever since the day I first met you ♪

655
00:43:16,600 --> 00:43:20,040
♪ You filled the missing space beside me ♪

656
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:21,560
(Just trust me.)

657
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,000
(I will always support you.)

